The cluster runs a reranker next to the chat and embedding nodes. Reranking has to come in through Skeid: client_auth (k90), routing over nodes, one usage event per forwarded request.

Routes (OpenAI face, behind the client gate): POST /v1/rerank, and POST /rerank as an alias of it.

Request, the shape vLLM, Cohere, Jina and infinity share: { model, query, documents, top_n, return_documents, ... }. Answer: { results: [ { index, relevance_score, document? } ], usage? }.

Upstream:
- default: the body goes to {node.url}/rerank unchanged (model replaced by the served model), the answer comes back unchanged. Covers vLLM (/v1/rerank), infinity started with --url-prefix /v1, Jina and Cohere. Skeid does not normalise what differs between them: `document` is {text} on vLLM and Cohere v1, a plain string on infinity; vLLM ignores return_documents and always returns the documents.
- node option `rerank_format: tei` for Hugging Face text-embeddings-inference, which has no Cohere-shaped route: POST <server root>/rerank with { query, texts, return_text, truncate? }, answer a bare array [ { index, score, text? } ]. Skeid translates both ways at the edge (ADR 0001): documents (strings or { text }) -> texts, return_documents -> return_text, the answer into results sorted by score, cut to top_n, relevance_score from score, document { text } when asked for. A new Protocol module, the only place TEI's field names appear.

Usage event (ADR 0004), endpoint /v1/rerank for both spellings of the route:
- new optional field `documents` (nullable): how many documents the request carried -- Skeid counts it itself, so it is there whatever the node reports
- tokens when the node reports them: usage.total_tokens / usage.prompt_tokens (vLLM, infinity, Jina), meta.tokens.input_tokens (Cohere), the x-compute-tokens response header (TEI). Rerank tokens are input tokens: a usage block with only total_tokens is recorded as input, so `input_per_million` prices it.
- stores and reports as for audio_seconds: jsonlog writes it, DBI gets a nullable column, totals / by key / by model carry it
- pricing per document or per search unit is not modelled: recorded, not priced

Done when: /v1/rerank and /rerank work against local fake upstreams in t/ (vLLM-shaped, infinity-shaped, TEI), two nodes of one model share the load, max_conns and health respected, request.start/request.finish paired on every exit path, client_auth 401 before anything is forwarded, a malformed body answers 400 without touching a node, existing behaviour unchanged, prove -lr t/ green. README, CONTEXT.md, POD, skeid-protocols skill follow.

Known gaps to leave as they are: infinity reports characters, not tokens, unless it runs with lengths_via_tokenize; no /v2/rerank; no streaming (the format has none).

