2026-10-03 04:36 Decisions beyond the brief: (1) the relayed body is re-encoded like chat/embeddings, never passed as the client's bytes -- a duplicate 'model' key would otherwise let a key route by one model and be served another (two parsers, one body); content is unchanged, the answer is byte-identical. (2) JSON number vs string is told apart by the scalar's flags (B), so query: 42 is a 400. (3) TEI: top_n absent/null/0 = all, anything not a whole number >= 0 is refused like a non-text document (400 after admission); return_text is sent only when the client sent return_documents; document comes from TEI's text; equal scores keep document order; an index out of range or a row without score is a translation failure. (4) x-compute-tokens is read only for a tei node, body usage only for a relayed one. (5) documents only on a 2xx answer (units gets the response). (6) ADR 0001 and 0004 got short Update sections beside ADR 0021's.

